 ## Paying and confirming
 
-- Before payment, send one question widget that restates the full itinerary, passenger names, fare, and total.
+- Before payment, send one question widget that restates the full itinerary, passenger names, fare, each extra added with its price, and the total. When you send an order card instead, its items are the fare for all travelers and then one line per extra with the price the review page shows, such as title "Checked bags" with detail "2 travelers, both flights";
+ taxes and fees are charges, and together they add up to the page's total. Nothing ships, so set `requiresShipping` false and leave out `shipTo`.
 - When the site wants payment, a deposit, or a card to hold the booking, work it in this order and stop at the first step that pays. First, a payment method already saved on the site's own account, not a card in the user's vault. Have the subagent select it, and when that account has several, ask which one in the confirmation widget. Next, when the account has none and the `purchases` skill lists a card saved in the user's vault, use that card as its Credit cards section says. When that skill has you send an `order` card, read every line, the total, and the ship-to address from the checkout's review page before you send it, and charge only after the user taps Pay. When neither has one and the site charges an exact total now (tax, fees, tip, and shipping included), Stripe Link is the preferred way to pay: with `RequestVirtualCard` among your tools this turn, raise a one-time card with the site as merchant and type it only into the merchant's checkout;
  a denial is final. Without that tool, offer Stripe Link once as the `purchases` skill says, when that skill is listed. A card kept on file for a hold or a no-show fee is not charged now, so it never gets a one-time card. Next, and right away whenever the user turns Link down, ignores the offer, or asks to use their own card, send the Secure Form (`RequestUserForm`, reason "checkout", the site's domain) for the card inputs the live checkout shows, such as card number, expiry, CVC, name, and billing ZIP;
